---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const privacySchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "IDSnap Privacy Policy & Data Safety",
  "description": "Official Privacy Policy for IDSnap. Explains our on-device architecture and compliance with Google Play Data Safety and Apple App Privacy guidelines.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IDSnap",
    "url": "https://idsnap.app"
  }
};
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy & Google Play Data Safety"
  description="IDSnap never uploads your documents and does not track you. Read our Privacy Policy and Google Play Data Safety specifications."
  schema={privacySchema}
>
  <div class="container legal-page-container">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <div class="badge-pill">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
        </svg>
        Your Documents Never Leave Your Phone
      </div>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy & Data Safety</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last Updated & Verified: September 25, 2026 • Effective Immediately</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Summary Box -->
    <div class="card-glass summary-box">
      <h3>The IDSnap Privacy Promise in Plain English</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>IDSnap is an accountless, on-device application.</strong> We do not operate document servers or cloud processing pipelines. Every scan, ID card collage, 2FA authenticator seed, and OCR extraction runs <strong>exclusively on your device</strong>. IDSnap is free and shows ads on a few screens; the ads are provided by Google, which may use your device's advertising ID. We never sell, rent or share your documents, IDs or codes: they never leave your phone.
      </p>
      <div class="promise-badges">
        <span class="promise-tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
          No Document Uploads
        </span>
        <span class="promise-tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
          No Account or Login Required
        </span>
        <span class="promise-tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
          No Analytics SDK of Our Own
        </span>
        <span class="promise-tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
          No Ads in Your Vault
        </span>
        <span class="promise-tag">
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
          Tools Work Offline
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section id="ads" class="legal-section">
        <h2>Ads and your privacy</h2>
        <p><strong>Your documents, IDs and codes never leave this phone. IDSnap is free and shows ads on a few screens; the ads are provided by Google, which may use your device's advertising ID.</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Who provides the ads:</strong> Google AdMob, through the Google Mobile Ads SDK built into the app. IDSnap's own code makes no network calls; the only connections are made by that SDK.</li>
          <li><strong>What the ad SDK may collect:</strong> your device's advertising ID and other device identifiers, your approximate location (worked out from your IP address), which ads were shown or tapped, and diagnostic data such as crash and performance information. Google uses this to show, measure and protect ads. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>What it never gets:</strong> your documents, scans, photos, ID cards, recognised text, file names, notes, 2FA secrets and codes, PINs or passwords. None of these are ever sent anywhere.</li>
          <li><strong>Where ads appear:</strong> on Home, the Tools list, some tool screens and after a tool has finished. Never in your ID Vault, on a document, in the authenticator, in secure notes, in the scanner or camera, on password or signature screens, or in Settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Your choices:</strong> in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland (and US states that require it) the app asks for your choice before any ad is requested, and you can change it at any time in Settings → Ad privacy choices. Without your consent to personalisation, IDSnap asks only for non-personalised ads. You can reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's settings (Android: Settings → Privacy → Ads).</li>
          <li><strong>iPhone:</strong> IDSnap does not ask to track you and does not use the advertising identifier (IDFA).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="google-play" class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Google Play Store Data Safety Declarations</h2>
        <p>
          For the purposes of the Google Play Console Data Safety questionnaire, IDSnap declares the following:
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="compliance-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Data Category</th>
                <th>Collected?</th>
                <th>Shared?</th>
                <th>Processing Type</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Personal IDs & Documents</strong> (Passports, Driver's Licenses, Cards)</td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td>Ephemeral local-only processing in on-device SQLite database.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>2FA Secrets & TOTP Seeds</strong></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td>Encrypted in Android KeyStore via <code>flutter_secure_storage</code>.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Photos & Camera Video Stream</strong></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td>Direct viewfinder feed; never transmitted over network.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Biometric Data</strong> (Fingerprint / Face ID)</td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td><span class="badge-pill badge-primary">No</span></td>
                <td>Evaluated entirely by OS hardware enclave; app receives only binary pass/fail token.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Device or Other IDs</strong> (advertising ID)</td>
                <td>Yes (by the Google ad SDK)</td>
                <td>Yes (Google, for advertising)</td>
                <td>Used to show, measure and protect ads. Reset or delete it in your phone's settings.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Approximate Location</strong> (from IP address)</td>
                <td>Yes (by the Google ad SDK)</td>
                <td>Yes (Google, for advertising)</td>
                <td>Coarse location for ad selection and fraud prevention. IDSnap never requests the location permission.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>App Interactions & Diagnostics</strong> (ads shown or tapped, crash and performance data)</td>
                <td>Yes (by the Google ad SDK)</td>
                <td>Yes (Google, for advertising and analytics)</td>
                <td>Collected by the ad SDK only. IDSnap has no analytics or crash-reporting SDK of its own.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="apple-privacy" class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Apple App Store Privacy Nutrition Labels</h2>
        <p>
          In accordance with Apple's App Privacy requirements for the iOS App Store:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Ads on iPhone:</strong> not shown yet. When they are, the labels will list the data Google's ad SDK collects (device ID, coarse location, advertising and usage data, diagnostics), used for third-party advertising and not linked to your identity.</li>
          <li><strong>Data Used to Track You:</strong> None. IDSnap does not ask for the advertising identifier (IDFA) and shows no tracking prompt.</li>
          <li><strong>Documents, IDs, 2FA secrets and notes:</strong> never collected.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="permissions" class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Device Permissions & How They Are Used</h2>
        <p>
          IDSnap requests only the minimum device permissions strictly required to perform local utility operations:
        </p>
        <div class="permissions-grid">
          <div class="permission-item">
            <h4><svg class="icon-inline" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M23 19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H3a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4l2-3h6l2 3h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="4"></circle></svg> Camera (<code>android.permission.CAMERA</code> / <code>NSCameraUsageDescription</code>)</h4>
            <p>Required to operate the document scanner, detect ID card borders, and scan 2FA setup QR codes. Captured frames stay in temporary device memory until processed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="permission-item">
            <h4><svg class="icon-inline" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M22 19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5l2 3h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"></path></svg> Storage / Photos (Scoped Photo Picker)</h4>
            <p>Used solely when you explicitly tap "Import photo" or "Import PDF" to select an image from your gallery, and when you tap "Save to device" to export the generated file to your local Downloads or Documents folder.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="permission-item">
            <h4><svg class="icon-inline" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="11" r="2"></circle><path d="M12 13v3"></path></svg> Biometrics (<code>USE_BIOMETRIC</code> / <code>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</code>)</h4>
            <p>Allows you to unlock your local ID Vault and reveal 2FA codes using your fingerprint or Face ID. Your biometric templates never leave the secure hardware enclave of your phone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="gdpr" class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. GDPR & CCPA/CPRA Compliance (Your Data Rights)</h2>
        <p>
          Because IDSnap stores your documents only on your device and has no user accounts:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right of Access & Portability (GDPR Art. 15/20):</strong> You have direct, unhindered access to all your files at all times through the in-app "Files" tab and the "Share / Save to Device" buttons.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure / "To Be Forgotten" (GDPR Art. 17):</strong> You can delete any individual document, 2FA account, or your entire database directly from the app settings, or by simply clearing the app data / uninstalling the app. No copies of your documents exist on any server. For ad data, reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's settings, change Settings → Ad privacy choices in the app, or use Google's controls.</li>
          <li><strong>Do Not Sell My Personal Information (CCPA):</strong> We never sell your documents or what is in your vault, which never leaves your phone. The Google ad SDK shares device identifiers and ad data with Google for advertising, which some US state laws treat as "sharing"; you can opt out of personalised ads in Settings → Ad privacy choices.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="children" class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Children's Privacy (COPPA Compliance)</h2>
        <p>
          IDSnap is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13. Documents are never transmitted off the device. The app shows ads from Google, so children under 13 should use it only with a parent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security-measures" class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Security of Your Local Data</h2>
        <p>
          Documents saved in IDSnap reside inside the app-private sandbox directory managed by the Android and iOS operating systems. Other third-party apps on your phone cannot read these files without root access or explicit OS file-sharing permissions granted by you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact-privacy" class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Contact & Verification Inquiries</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or wish to conduct a technical security audit, contact our compliance team:
        </p>
        <div class="contact-box">
          <p><strong>Privacy & Security Team:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@idsnap.app">privacy@idsnap.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>Developer Support:</strong> <a href="/contact">Visit Support Center</a></p>
          <p><strong>Security Architecture Guide:</strong> <a href="/security">Read Technical Verification</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-container {
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }

  .summary-box {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    background-color: var(--primary-container);
    border: 1px solid rgba(36, 87, 214, 0.2);
  }

  .summary-box h3 {
    color: var(--on-primary-container);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .summary-box p {
    color: var(--on-primary-container);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .promise-badges {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .promise-tag {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--outline-variant);
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .compliance-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .compliance-table th, .compliance-table td {
    padding: 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .compliance-table th {
    background-color: var(--surface-container-high);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--on-surface);
  }

  .permissions-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .permission-item {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .permission-item h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--on-surface);
  }

  .contact-box {
    background-color: var(--surface-container);
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
